{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbpLCbVAbiviAyqHJsbu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Byp1JEsibfeKKNos1mrTEa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work/run; cat > result.json <<'E'\n{\n \"candidate\": \"silicon (diamond cubic)\",\n \"family\": \"elemental semiconductor\",\n \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"lattice_constant\",\n \"value\": 5.467,\n \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n \"uncertainty\": 0.002,\n \"method\": {\n  \"engine\": \"ALCHEMI toolkit environment (mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator, CUDA, float64)\",\n  \"model\": \"MACE-MPA-0 (medium)\",\n  \"protocol\": \"static 0 K E(V) scan of the ideal diamond-cubic cell (isotropic strain, no thermal/zero-point contributions) followed by an equation-of-state fit; 3 strain ranges (+/-2% with 11 points, +/-4% with 11, +/-6% with 15) x 3 cell sizes (8, 64, 216 atoms) x 3 EOS forms (Birch-Murnaghan, Vinet, Murnaghan)\",\n  \"ensemble\": null,\n  \"timestep_fs\": null,\n  \"n_atoms\": 8,\n  \"sim_length_ps\": null,\n  \"eos_forms\": [\"birchmurnaghan\", \"vinet\", \"murnaghan\"],\n  \"supercells_checked\": [8, 64, 216],\n  \"bulk_modulus_GPa\": 87.6\n },\n \"flags\": [],\n \"note\": \"Value is the +/-2% strain-window fit (5.4673 A, all 3 EOS forms within 0.0001 A). The mean over all 27 fits is 5.4665 A, range 5.4653-5.4673 A. Wider windows shift a0 down by up to 0.002 A because of EOS-form bias. Cell size has no effect (<1e-5 A). The uncertainty of 0.002 A covers ONLY the numerical/fit spread (EOS form, strain window, cell size). It does NOT cover model error. PREMISE: well-posed. A static EOS gives the 0 K classical lattice constant of a perfect crystal. Si is in the training domain of MACE-MPA-0, which is trained on PBE data (MPtrj+sAlex). So the number targets PBE, not experiment. VALIDATION (same model, same protocol): fcc Cu/Al/Ag give 3.639/4.038/4.162 A. That matches the PBE values 3.642/4.042/4.147 A tabulated in arXiv:2604.07046 (Table C.1, LC20 set) to within -0.1%/-0.1%/+0.4%. The same table gives experimental reference values of 3.595/4.018/4.062 A, so MACE is +1.2%/+0.5%/+2.4% vs experiment, the known PBE overestimate. Also computed, but with no sourced reference on hand: Ge 5.720 A (PBE is known to strongly overestimate Ge), diamond C 3.578 A, B(Si) = 87.6 GPa. COMPARISON: CODATA 2018/2022 Si lattice parameter is 5.431020511(89) A (vacuum, 22.5 C; NIST physics.nist.gov/cuu/pdf/xray_2018.pdf). This result is +0.036 A (+0.66%) above it. That is consistent with the PBE-type bias seen in the validation set. Zero-point and thermal-expansion effects (0 K static vs 295 K) are much smaller than this offset in Si and were not computed. Realistic error vs experiment is therefore about +0.5 to +1% (+0.03 to +0.05 A), dominated by the PBE reference of the model.\"\n}\nE\ncd /work; ./board post property_result @run/result.json --parent 28d912e0-d10b-4d9a-aeca-b48d51edabcc; ./board show | head -8"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":898,"cache_read_input_tokens":40877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":898,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da0dc3b6-c5de-4e9f-8234-2ef78e8ae4a4","uuid":"c6d2c4ce-f22e-4d42-906c-1b5028d9c1ce","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:30:58.413Z","request_id":"req_011CgbpLCDQpnzG3Krq2Naab","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Byp1JEsibfeKKNos1mrTEa":{"command":"cd /work/run; cat > result.json <<'E'\n{\n \"candidate\": \"silicon (diamond cubic)\",\n \"family\": \"elemental semiconductor\",\n \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"lattice_constant\",\n \"value\": 5.467,\n \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n \"uncertainty\": 0.002,\n \"method\": {\n  \"engine\": \"AL